From f31863228f1517066b0e6d2684d7fbd1e20ec64e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:18:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] deploy: fix verified failures F1-F3, unmask I8, harden
 build proxy

Root-cause fixes for the independent deploy verification of 22d5d3f
(test_worker, 2026-09-28; smoke full with the I1 proposal: 41 PASS / 3 FAIL).

- F2 (S34 FAIL, S21 false PASS): admin "/" answered
  "307 Location: https://localhost:3100/zh-CN" through Caddy. Next builds
  its request origin from HOSTNAME=127.0.0.1, while request.nextUrl
  canonicalises 127.x to "localhost", so Next could not relativise the
  proxy.ts locale redirect. compose.yml now wires HOSTNAME=localhost and
  admin.Dockerfile starts node with --dns-result-order=ipv4first, so the
  server still binds 127.0.0.1. Checked locally with the built image:
  the redirect is now "Location: /zh-CN". S21 now asserts the Location
  stays on the public origin and that the target returns 200 with
  X-Frame-Options DENY. S34 asserts the final host and a 200 status.
- F3 (S39 FAIL): post_checks waited for a ready token logged after the
  script started, and a no-op `up -d` never prints one. The token must
  now appear in `docker logs --since <.State.StartedAt>`, and every lc-*
  container must run :$IMAGE_TAG. S39 now covers four rollback paths:
  the no-op, a different tag (containers are recreated), back to the
  original tag, and a refusal when the ledger changed.
- F1 (S08 false negative): compare the binary names against
  go.Dockerfile GO_CMDS + lcentry instead of counting with a regex that
  also matched the app/bin/ directory entry.
- I8 unmasked: the new case S29m compares the live media gate with the
  restored one. It records BLOCKED (REQUIRES_INTEGRATOR I8) instead of
  hiding the defect inside the S29 PASS. S31 records media_plan.
- I1: go.Dockerfile checks every cmd/<name> before compiling. A missing
  cmd/migrate now fails in under 1 s instead of after five builds.
- build-images.sh: a loopback HTTPS_PROXY is unreachable from BuildKit
  RUN steps (checked locally). LC_BUILD_NETWORK=auto builds with
  --network host only in that case and logs the variable name, never
  its value.
- Docs: README deviations 10-14 and the status matrix; runbooks cover
  the post-check semantics, the no-op rollback, S29m and an admin
  redirect triage entry.

No production deploy performed. cmd/migrate (I1), the media-gate
migration (I8) and a path-only redirect in apps/admin/proxy.ts are
outside deploy/** and stay REQUIRES_INTEGRATOR / app owner.

